"label": "Use the ratio of speeds",
"explanation": "By the meeting, \\(A\\) has ridden \\(60-12=48\\) miles, while \\(B\\) has ridden \\(60+12=72\\) miles. Since their elapsed times are equal, their speeds have the same ratio as these distances:\n\\[\n\\text{speed of }A:\\text{speed of }B=48:72=2:3.\n\\]\nThe difference between the speeds is therefore one ratio part. That part equals \\(4\\) mph, so \\(A\\)'s two parts equal \\(2\\cdot4=8\\) mph, choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
