"explanation": "A logarithm tells us which exponent produces its argument. Thus \\(\\log_6 x=2.5\\) means \\(x=6^{2.5}\\). Writing \\(2.5=2+\\tfrac12\\) separates an integer power from a square root:\n\\[\nx=6^{2+1/2}=6^2\\sqrt6=36\\sqrt6.\n\\]\nThis value is positive, as required for the logarithm. The answer is \\(36\\sqrt6\\), choice C.",
