"label": "Eliminate both variables",
"explanation": "The second equation's left side is exactly twice the first equation's left side. Therefore, any solution of the first equation must satisfy\n\\[\n4x-6y=2(7)=14.\n\\]\nBut the second equation requires the same expression to equal \\(20\\). Subtracting these requirements gives the impossible equality \\(0=6\\). Thus no pair \\((x,y)\\) satisfies both equations, so the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
