"label": "Add moving time and stopped time",
"explanation": "The total elapsed time includes both travel and stops. At \\(40\\) miles per hour, traveling \\(a\\) miles takes \\(a/40\\) hours.\n\nThe \\(n\\) stops last \\(m\\) minutes each, so together they take \\(mn\\) minutes. Since there are \\(60\\) minutes in an hour, this is \\(mn/60\\) hours. Adding the two times gives\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{40}+\\frac{mn}{60}\n=\\frac{3a+2mn}{120}.\n\\]\nThe trip takes \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3a+2mn}{120}}\\) hours, choice A.",
