"id": "solve-and-check-slopes",
"label": "Check the side slopes",
"explanation": "The given sum of squares and product let us find the sum and difference of the coordinates:\n\\[\n(x+y)^2=x^2+y^2+2xy=49,\n\\]\n\\[\n(x-y)^2=x^2+y^2-2xy=1.\n\\]\nTaking both signs gives \\(x+y=\\pm7\\) and \\(x-y=\\pm1\\). The four resulting pairs, in order around the resulting quadrilateral, are\n\\[\nA=(3,4),\\quad B=(4,3),\n\\]\n\\[\nC=(-3,-4),\\quad D=(-4,-3).\n\\]\nThese four pairs all satisfy the original equations, and the four possible sign combinations show that the list is exhaustive.\n\nAll four side slopes are defined. Calculating them gives\n\\[\nm_{AB}=m_{CD}=-1,\n\\qquad\nm_{BC}=m_{DA}=1.\n\\]\nOpposite sides are therefore parallel. Adjacent sides are perpendicular because their slopes have product \\(-1\\). Thus the quadrilateral is a parallelogram with a right angle, so it is a rectangle.\n\nIts adjacent side lengths are\n\\[\nAB=\\sqrt{(4-3)^2+(3-4)^2}=\\sqrt2\n\\]\nand\n\\[\nBC=\\sqrt{(-3-4)^2+(-4-3)^2}=7\\sqrt2.\n\\]\nThese are unequal, so it is not a square. The most specific choice is D, a rectangle.",
