"rejectedAnswers": [],
"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "Average speed is total distance divided by total elapsed time. The two legs have equal distances, but the slower return takes longer.\n\nWe may calculate using \\(450\\) miles for each leg: multiplying both actual leg distances by a common positive factor also multiplies both travel times by that factor, leaving the average speed unchanged. This distance makes both times whole numbers:\n\\[\n\\text{outbound time}=\\frac{450}{50}=9\\text{ hours},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{return time}=\\frac{450}{45}=10\\text{ hours}.\n\\]\nThe entire journey covers \\(900\\) miles in \\(19\\) hours, so its average speed is\n\\[\n\\frac{900}{19}=47\\frac7{19}\\text{ mph}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice A.",
