"rejectedAnswers": [],
"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "Express each rectangle dimension in terms of \\(x\\), then add them. For a nondegenerate rectangle, \\(0<x<12\\).\n\nOpposite sides of a rectangle are equal, so\n\\[\nNP=MC=AC-AM=12-x.\n\\]\nTo find \\(MN\\), compare triangles \\(AMN\\) and \\(ACB\\). They share the angle at \\(A\\), and both are right triangles, at \\(M\\) and \\(C\\), respectively. They are therefore similar, giving\n\\[\n\\frac{MN}{BC}=\\frac{AM}{AC},\n\\qquad MN=5\\cdot\\frac{x}{12}=\\frac{5x}{12}.\n\\]\nThus\n\\[\ny=MN+NP\n=\\frac{5x}{12}+12-x\n=\\frac{144-7x}{12}.\n\\]\nIf endpoints are admitted as collapsed rectangles, \\(x=0\\) gives \\(y=12\\), and \\(x=12\\) gives \\(y=5\\), also agreeing with this formula. The answer is \\(\\boxed{y=\\frac{144-7x}{12}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{C}\\).",
