"id": "triangle-area-decomposition",
"label": "Use the areas on either side of CN",
"explanation": "Drawing \\(CN\\) divides the whole triangle into two triangles whose heights are the rectangle dimensions. This gives an equation connecting those dimensions.\n\nFor \\(0<x<12\\), write \\(h=MN\\) and \\(w=NP\\). The rectangle gives\n\\[\nw=MC=12-x.\n\\]\nThe triangles \\(ACN\\) and \\(BCN\\) together fill \\(ABC\\), with no overlapping interiors. Using bases \\(AC\\) and \\(BC\\), their respective heights are \\(h\\) and \\(w\\). Therefore\n\\[\n\\frac12\\cdot12h+\\frac12\\cdot5w\n=\\frac12\\cdot12\\cdot5.\n\\]\nSubstitute \\(w=12-x\\) and multiply by \\(2\\):\n\\[\n12h+5(12-x)=60,\n\\qquad h=\\frac{5x}{12}.\n\\]\nIt follows that\n\\[\ny=h+w=\\frac{5x}{12}+12-x\n=\\frac{144-7x}{12}.\n\\]\nAt the collapsed endpoint cases, \\(x=0\\) gives dimensions \\(0,12\\), and \\(x=12\\) gives dimensions \\(5,0\\); both satisfy the formula. The answer is \\(\\boxed{y=\\frac{144-7x}{12}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{C}\\).",
