"id": "double-root-condition",
"label": "Use the repeated-root condition",
"explanation": "When the vertex of this downward-opening parabola lies on the \\(x\\)-axis, the parabola meets the axis at exactly one point. Thus\n\\[\n-x^2+bx-8=0\n\\]\nhas a repeated real root. A quadratic has a repeated real root exactly when its discriminant is zero, so\n\\[\nb^2-4(-1)(-8)=b^2-32=0.\n\\]\nConsequently \\(b=\\pm\\sqrt{32}=\\pm4\\sqrt2\\). Conversely, either value makes the discriminant zero, so the single intercept is the vertex. Both values are irrational, because dividing either by the corresponding nonzero rational factor \\(4\\) or \\(-4\\) gives the irrational number \\(\\sqrt2\\). Therefore \\(b\\) may be positive or negative and must be irrational, choice D.",
