"label": "Use an altitude and the 30° right-triangle property",
"explanation": "The \\(60^\\circ\\) angle suggests drawing an altitude, which creates a right triangle with a \\(30^\\circ\\) angle. Let \\(AB=80\\), \\(\\angle BAC=60^\\circ\\), and \\(AC=t\\). Then \\(BC=90-t\\), with \\(0<t<90\\).\n\nDrop the perpendicular \\(CH\\) to the line \\(AB\\). Because the angle at \\(A\\) is acute, \\(H\\) lies on ray \\(AB\\). In right triangle \\(ACH\\), the angle at \\(C\\) is \\(30^\\circ\\), so\n\\[\nAH=\\frac t2,\n\\qquad CH^2=t^2-\\left(\\frac t2\\right)^2=\\frac{3t^2}{4}.\n\\]\nAlso, \\(AH<45<80\\), so \\(H\\) lies between \\(A\\) and \\(B\\). Applying the Pythagorean theorem to \\(BCH\\) gives\n\\[\n(90-t)^2=\\left(80-\\frac t2\\right)^2+\\frac{3t^2}{4}\n=6400-80t+t^2.\n\\]\nExpanding the left side and canceling \\(t^2\\), we obtain\n\\[\n8100-180t=6400-80t,\n\\qquad 100t=1700.\n\\]\nThus \\(t=17\\) and \\(90-t=73\\). These are positive and satisfy \\(17+73>80\\), so the resulting triangle is nondegenerate. Its sides are \\(17,73,80\\), and the shortest is \\(\\boxed{17}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
