"label": "Count the gaps",
"explanation": "The first strike occurs precisely at the starting time, so the elapsed time comes from the gaps between strikes. Six strikes have \\(6-1=5\\) gaps. Since these equal gaps take \\(5\\) seconds altogether, each gap lasts \\(5\\div5=1\\) second.\n\nTwelve strikes have \\(12-1=11\\) gaps, so they take \\(11\\cdot1=11\\) seconds. The answer is \\(\\boxed{11}\\), choice C.",
"directNodeIds": [
"cnm_p151"
],
