"explanation": "An arithmetic progression adds the same number at every step. The difference between the first two terms is\n\\[\n(x+1)-(x-1)=2.\n\\]\nThe third term must therefore be \\((x+1)+2=x+3\\). Equating this with the given third term gives\n\\[\n2x+3=x+3,\n\\]\nso \\(x=0\\). Substituting gives the terms \\(-1,1,3\\), which do have common difference \\(2\\). Thus \\(x=0\\), choice B.",
