"explanation": "Let \\(M\\) be the midpoint of the fixed segment \\(AB\\), and let \\(G\\) be the intersection of the medians. The useful fixed point is \\(M\\): although \\(C\\) moves, \\(M\\) does not.\n\nThe centroid divides the median \\(CM\\) in the ratio \\(CG:GM=2:1\\). Consequently, \\(G\\) lies on the ray from \\(M\\) through \\(C\\), with\n\\[\nMG=\\frac13MC.\n\\]\nThus \\(G\\) is obtained from \\(C\\) by a dilation centered at \\(M\\) with scale factor \\(1/3\\). A dilation maps a line not through its center to a parallel line, and maps a line through its center to itself. Therefore \\(G\\) moves on a straight line, choice D.\n\nBecause \\(ABC\\) must remain a nondegenerate triangle, positions of \\(C\\) on the line \\(AB\\) are excluded. If the path crosses \\(AB\\), the corresponding centroid position is omitted from the supporting straight line.",
