"label": "Use logarithms as exponents",
"explanation": "By definition, \\(b=\\log_2 15\\) means \\(2^b=15\\). To find \\(a\\), we seek the exponent to which \\(8\\) must be raised to obtain \\(225=15^2\\). Using positive-base real exponent laws,\n\\[\n8^{2b/3}=(2^3)^{2b/3}\n=2^{2b}=(2^b)^2\n=15^2=225.\n\\]\nSince \\(\\log_8 225\\) is the unique exponent producing \\(225\\) from base \\(8\\), we obtain \\(a=\\boxed{2b/3}\\), choice B.",
