"label": "Check the denominator and the values",
"explanation": "A point on this graph must have \\(x+1\\ne0\\), because division by zero is undefined. At \\(x=-1\\), the denominator is zero, so \\((-1,1)\\) cannot lie on the graph.\n\nFor completeness, the other listed inputs give\n\\[\n\\frac0{0+1}=0,\\qquad\n\\frac{-1/2}{1/2}=-1,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{1/2}{3/2}=\\frac13,\\qquad\n\\frac{-2}{-1}=2.\n\\]\nThus A, B, C, and E lie on the graph. The point that does not is \\((-1,1)\\), choice D.",
