"id": "double-root-discriminant",
"label": "Use the discriminant",
"explanation": "Equating the two expressions for \\(y\\) gives\n\\[\n x^2-3x-k=0.\n\\]\nEvery root of this equation determines exactly one common solution by \\(y=x^2\\). Thus the requested identical solutions correspond to a repeated root of this quadratic.\n\nFor a quadratic \\(Ax^2+Bx+C=0\\), with \\(A\\ne0\\), the roots coincide exactly when its discriminant \\(B^2-4AC\\) is zero. Here the discriminant is\n\\[\n (-3)^2-4(1)(-k)=9+4k.\n\\]\nHence \\(9+4k=0\\), giving \\(k=-\\frac94\\), choice D.",
