"question": "Given the line \\(y=\\dfrac34x+6\\) and a line \\(L\\) parallel to the given line and \\(4\\) units from it. A possible equation for \\(L\\) is:",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(y=\\dfrac34x+1\\)",
"B": "\\(y=\\dfrac34x\\)",
"C": "\\(y=\\dfrac34x-\\dfrac23\\)",
"D": "\\(y=\\dfrac34x-1\\)",
"E": "\\(y=\\dfrac34x+2\\)"
},
"choiceOrder": [
"A",
"B",
"C",
"D",
"E"
],
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "A",
"acceptedResponses": [
"A"
],
"rejectedAnswers": [],
"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "The distance between parallel lines is measured perpendicularly. Since the given line has slope \\(3/4\\), a perpendicular has slope \\(-4/3\\). Moving 3 units right and 4 units down follows this perpendicular direction and covers \\(\\sqrt{3^2+4^2}=5\\) units.\n\nStart at \\(P=(0,6)\\) on the given line. Scaling that movement by \\(4/5\\) gives a perpendicular step of length 4, reaching\n\\[\nQ=\\left(\\frac{12}{5},6-\\frac{16}{5}\\right)\n=\\left(\\frac{12}{5},\\frac{14}{5}\\right).\n\\]\nThe parallel line through \\(Q\\) has slope \\(3/4\\), so its equation is\n\\[\ny-\\frac{14}{5}\n=\\frac34\\left(x-\\frac{12}{5}\\right).\n\\]\nThis simplifies to \\(y=\\frac34x+1\\). Because \\(PQ\\) is perpendicular to both lines and has length 4, this line satisfies the required distance.\n\nTaking the opposite perpendicular step reaches \\(R=(-12/5,46/5)\\). The parallel line through \\(R\\) has y-intercept\n\\[\n\\frac{46}{5}-\\frac34\\left(-\\frac{12}{5}\\right)=11.\n\\]\nAny required line must intersect the perpendicular through \\(P\\) at distance 4 from \\(P\\), so these two points give all possibilities. Only the intercept 1 is listed. Thus the answer is \\(\\boxed{y=\\frac34x+1}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
