"explanation": "By definition, \\(\\log_{10}9\\) is the exponent to which \\(10\\) must be raised to obtain \\(9\\). The logarithm is defined because its argument is positive and its base is positive and different from \\(1\\). Therefore\n\\[\n10^{\\log_{10}9}=9.\n\\]\nThe given equation becomes \\(8x+5=9\\). Subtracting \\(5\\) and dividing by \\(8\\) gives\n\\[\nx=\\frac{9-5}{8}=\\frac12.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\frac12\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
