"label": "Apply the rule from the inside outward",
"explanation": "The parentheses require us to evaluate \\(4*4\\) first. Applying the given rule,\n\\[\n4*4=\\frac{4\\cdot4}{4+4}=2.\n\\]\nNow use that result as the second input:\n\\[\n4*(4*4)=4*2=\\frac{4\\cdot2}{4+2}=\\frac43.\n\\]\nBoth denominators are positive, so both applications are defined. The answer is \\(\\frac43\\), choice C.",
