"label": "Cancel adjacent pairs",
"explanation": "The terms are \\(-1,1,-1,1,\\ldots\\), so every adjacent pair has sum \\(0\\). If \\(n\\) is even, all terms pair off. If \\(n\\) is odd, one final \\(-1\\) remains. Therefore\n\\[\nf(n)=\\begin{cases}\n0,&n\\text{ even},\\\\\n-\\dfrac1n,&n\\text{ odd}.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nEvery positive integer is either even or odd, so these cases give all possible values. The value \\(0\\) occurs, for example, at \\(n=2\\); each negative value occurs at its corresponding positive odd index. Hence the exact range is\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,-1,-\\tfrac13,-\\tfrac15,\\ldots\\}}.\n\\]\nChoice C is the intended answer only when its \\(-1/n\\) is restricted to odd \\(n\\). As printed, it does not state that restriction. In particular, \\(-1/2\\) cannot occur: a negative output requires odd \\(n\\), whereas \\(-1/n=-1/2\\) would require \\(n=2\\).",
