"label": "Subtract the values at opposite inputs",
"explanation": "At \\(x=1\\) and \\(x=-1\\), the squared terms agree. Subtracting the corresponding function values will therefore cancel the terms involving \\(a\\) and \\(c\\). Substitution gives\n\\[\ny_1=a+b+c,\\qquad y_2=a-b+c.\n\\]\nConsequently,\n\\[\n-6=y_1-y_2\n=(a+b+c)-(a-b+c)=2b.\n\\]\nDividing by \\(2\\) yields \\(b=-3\\), choice A.",
