"solution": "Measuring horizontal distance from the center puts the parabola in a simple form. Take \\(M=(0,0)\\), with heights measured above \\(AB\\). The vertex is \\(C=(0,16)\\), and the span of \\(40\\) inches places the endpoints at \\((-20,0)\\) and \\((20,0)\\).\n\nA downward-opening parabola with this vertex has equation\n\\[\ny=16-kx^2,\\qquad -20\\le x\\le20,\n\\]\nwhere \\(k>0\\). Substituting the endpoint \\((20,0)\\) gives\n\\[\n0=16-400k,\n\\qquad k=\\frac1{25}.\n\\]\nAt either point \\(5\\) inches horizontally from \\(M\\), we have \\(x=\\pm5\\), so\n\\[\ny=16-\\frac{5^2}{25}=15.\n\\]\nThe height is \\(15\\) inches, choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
