"label": "Simplify the powers before dividing",
"explanation": "The defining identity \\(i^2=-1\\) gives \\(i^4=(i^2)^2=1\\). Substituting these values makes the numerator vanish:\n\\[\nf(i)=\\frac{i^4+i^2}{i+1}\n=\\frac{1-1}{1+i}=0.\n\\]\nThe denominator \\(1+i\\) is nonzero because its imaginary part is \\(1\\). Therefore \\(\\boxed{f(i)=0}\\), choice D.",
