"label": "Make the divisor vanish",
"explanation": "Because the divisor \\(x+1\\) has degree \\(1\\), the remainder is a constant \\(r\\). Write the division identity as\n\\[\nx^{51}+51=(x+1)Q(x)+r,\n\\]\nwhere \\(Q(x)\\) is the polynomial quotient. Setting \\(x=-1\\) makes the term containing the quotient vanish, leaving\n\\[\nr=(-1)^{51}+51=-1+51=50.\n\\]\nThe remainder is \\(\\boxed{50}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
