"explanation": "Give the four variable names shorter symbols: let \\(w,h,i,s\\) stand for whatsis, whosis, is, and so, respectively. In the verbal arithmetic, “so and so” means \\(s+s=2s\\). The opening rule says that\n\\[\nw=s\\quad\\text{when}\\quad h=i\\ \\text{and}\\ 2s=is.\n\\]\nThe situation we are asked about has\n\\[\nh=s,\\qquad 2s=s^2,\\qquad i=2.\n\\]\nBecause \\(s>0\\), dividing \\(2s=s^2\\) by \\(s\\) is valid and gives \\(s=2\\). Hence \\(h=2\\) as well.\n\nWe can now check both conditions of the opening rule: \\(h=i=2\\), and \\(2s=4=is\\). Therefore that rule gives \\(w=s=2\\). The requested product is\n\\[\nhw=2\\cdot2=4=s+s.\n\\]\nThis is “so and so,” choice \\(\\boxed{\\mathrm{E}}\\).",
