"explanation": "Every denominator divides \\(64\\), so we can add the six fractions using that common denominator. Their sum is\n\\[\n\\frac{96+80+72+68+66+65}{64}\n=\\frac{447}{64}.\n\\]\nSince \\(7=448/64\\), the original expression equals\n\\[\n\\frac{447}{64}-\\frac{448}{64}\n=\\boxed{-\\frac1{64}},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
