"explanation": "The perpendicular diameters make \\(\\angle PQC=90^\\circ\\), so triangle \\(PQC\\) is a right triangle. Since \\(\\angle QPC=60^\\circ\\), its angle at \\(C\\) is \\(30^\\circ\\).\n\nLet \\(PQ=x>0\\) and let the circle's radius be \\(r>0\\). Then \\(QC=AQ=r\\). The side opposite the \\(30^\\circ\\) angle is half the hypotenuse, so \\(PC=2x\\). The Pythagorean theorem now gives\n\\[\nx^2+r^2=(2x)^2,\n\\qquad r^2=3x^2.\n\\]\nBecause both lengths are positive, \\(r=\\sqrt3x\\). Thus\n\\[\n\\frac{PQ}{AQ}=\\frac{x}{r}\n=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\n=\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice B.",
