"explanation": "A line's slope is the tangent of its inclination, so the doubled angle suggests the tangent addition formula. Let \\(\\theta\\) be the inclination of \\(L_2\\); the inclination of \\(L_1\\) is \\(2\\theta\\). Inclinations lie in \\([0,180^\\circ)\\), and \\(L_1\\) is not horizontal, so \\(0<\\theta<90^\\circ\\). Consequently \\(n>0\\). Since \\(m=4n>0\\), the inclination \\(2\\theta\\) is also acute.\n\nWe have \\(n=\\tan\\theta\\), and tangent addition gives\n\\[\nm=\\tan(2\\theta)=\\frac{2n}{1-n^2}.\n\\]\nThe denominator is nonzero because \\(2\\theta\\) is not a right angle. Substituting \\(m=4n\\) and dividing by \\(n\\ne0\\) gives\n\\[\n4=\\frac{2}{1-n^2},\n\\qquad n^2=\\frac12.\n\\]\nTherefore\n\\[\nmn=4n^2=2,\n\\]\nwhich is choice C.",
