"label": "Factor the polynomial",
"explanation": "Divisibility by \\((x-r)^2\\) means that \\(r\\) is a repeated root. The choices cluster near \\(1.5\\), so testing the simple value \\(3/2\\) is useful. For\n\\[\nP(x)=8x^3-4x^2-42x+45,\n\\]\nwe find\n\\[\nP\\left(\\frac32\\right)=27-9-63+45=0.\n\\]\nThus \\(2x-3\\) is a factor. Polynomial division gives\n\\[\nP(x)=(2x-3)(4x^2+4x-15).\n\\]\nThe remaining quadratic factors as\n\\[\n4x^2+4x-15=(2x-3)(2x+5),\n\\]\nas expansion verifies. Therefore\n\\[\nP(x)=(2x-3)^2(2x+5).\n\\]\nThe root \\(-5/2\\) occurs only once, whereas \\(3/2\\) occurs twice, so \\(r=3/2=1.50\\).\n\nThe distance from \\(1.50\\) to \\(1.52\\) is \\(0.02\\); every other listed number is at least \\(0.08\\) away. The closest number is therefore \\(\\boxed{1.52}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
