"label": "Find the side squared directly",
"explanation": "Since \\(E\\) lies on side \\(AB\\) of the square, \\(EB\\perp BC\\). Thus triangle \\(EBC\\) is right at \\(B\\), with hypotenuse \\(EC=2\\) and leg \\(EB=1\\). The Pythagorean theorem gives\n\\[\nBC^2=EC^2-EB^2=2^2-1^2=3.\n\\]\nThe square's area is its side length squared, so the area is already \\(\\boxed{3}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
