"label": "Group the base-three digits in pairs",
"explanation": "Because \\(9=3^2\\), moving one place in base nine has the same effect as moving two places in base three. We can therefore convert by grouping base-three digits in pairs from the right:\n\\[\n12\\mid11\\mid22\\mid11\\mid12\\mid22\\mid11\\mid11\\mid22\\mid22.\n\\]\nEach pair has a value from \\(0\\) through \\(8\\), so it becomes one valid base-nine digit. There are \\(20\\) base-three digits, and the leading pair is \\(12\\). Its value is\n\\[\n1\\cdot3+2=5.\n\\]\nThus the first base-nine digit is \\(5\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
