"explanation": "Multiplying the divisor by \\(x\\) produces the leading term \\(x^3\\), so subtracting this multiple reveals the remainder:\n\\[x^3-2-x(x^2-2)=x^3-2-x^3+2x=2x-2.\\]\nThus\n\\[x^3-2=x(x^2-2)+(2x-2).\\]\nThe remaining polynomial has degree one, which is less than the divisor's degree two, so division is complete. The remainder is \\(2x-2\\), choice E.",
