"solution": "Count the remaining outside surface and the newly exposed tunnel walls separately. The three perpendicular tunnels overlap exactly in the central cube of side \\(1\\) meter.\n\nEach of the original six faces has area \\(3^2=9\\) square meters and loses a square opening of area \\(1\\). Thus the remaining exterior contributes\n\\[\n6(9-1)=48\n\\]\nsquare meters.\n\nOutside the central cube, the tunnels form six arms, one leading to each face. Centering leaves each arm with length \\((3-1)/2=1\\) meter. Each arm has four square walls, each \\(1\\) meter by \\(1\\) meter, so the interior area is\n\\[\n6\\cdot4\\cdot1=24\n\\]\nsquare meters. Both ends of each arm are open. All six faces of the central cube open into these arms, so there is no additional wall at the central crossing.\n\nThese outside faces and interior wall panels cover the entire surface, and distinct panels share at most edges, which contribute no area. The total is\n\\[\n48+24=\\boxed{72\\text{ m}^2},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
