"label": "Use odd and even numbers",
"explanation": "The only even prime is \\(2\\), because every larger even number has \\(2\\) as a factor besides \\(1\\) and itself. If \\(p>2\\), then \\(q>p\\) makes both primes odd. Their sum \\(r=p+q\\) would then be even and greater than \\(2\\), contradicting that \\(r\\) is prime. Therefore \\(p=2\\). These conditions are possible, as \\(2+3=5\\). The answer is \\(\\boxed{2}\\), choice A.",
