"explanation": "Pair factors of \\(2\\) with factors of \\(5\\), because each pair produces a factor of \\(10\\). Since \\(4^{16}=2^{32}\\), there are \\(25\\) such pairs and \\(7\\) factors of \\(2\\) left:\n\\[\n4^{16}5^{25}\n=2^7(2^{25}5^{25})\n=2^7\\cdot10^{25}\n=128\\cdot10^{25}.\n\\]\nMultiplying a positive integer by \\(10^{25}\\) appends \\(25\\) zeros to its decimal representation. Thus the three digits of \\(128\\), followed by those zeros, give \\(3+25=\\boxed{28}\\) digits, choice D.",
