"label": "Combine the products into one cosine",
"explanation": "The two products are the terms in the cosine addition formula\n\\[\n\\cos(A+B)=\\cos A\\cos B-\\sin A\\sin B.\n\\]\nMoving the sine product to the other side of the given equation therefore gives\n\\[\n0=\\cos2x\\cos3x-\\sin2x\\sin3x=\\cos5x.\n\\]\nSince \\(\\cos90^\\circ=0\\), choosing \\(5x=90^\\circ\\) makes the equation true. Thus one value is \\(\\boxed{18^\\circ}\\), choice A.",
