"solution": "The perimeter includes both the curved boundary and the two straight edges of the mouth. Each straight edge is a radius, so together they have length \\(2\\) cm.\n\nThe remaining arc has central angle \\(360^\\circ-60^\\circ=300^\\circ\\), so it is \\(300/360=5/6\\) of the full circumference. Since the radius is \\(1\\) cm, its length is\n\\[\n\\frac56(2\\pi\\cdot1)=\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\text{ cm}.\n\\]\nAdding the two radii gives the perimeter\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{5\\pi}{3}+2\\text{ cm}},\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
