"solution": "The only new side of the remaining quadrilateral is \\(DE\\), so first find its length. Since \\(ABC\\) is equilateral and \\(D\\) and \\(E\\) lie on \\(AB\\) and \\(CB\\), respectively, \\(\\angle DBE=60^\\circ\\). Also, \\(BD=BE=1\\). An isosceles triangle with a \\(60^\\circ\\) vertex angle is equilateral, so \\(DE=1\\).\n\nThe two shortened sides have lengths\n\\[\nAD=3-1=2,\\qquad EC=3-1=2.\n\\]\nAdding the four sides along the boundary of \\(ADEC\\) gives\n\\[\nAD+DE+EC+CA=2+1+2+3=8.\n\\]\nThe perimeter is \\(\\boxed{8}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
