"id": "base-and-height",
"label": "Minimize the perpendicular height",
"explanation": "Since side \\(AB\\) is fixed, minimizing the area amounts to minimizing the positive perpendicular distance from \\(C\\) to line \\(AB\\). The fixed base has length\n\\[\nAB=\\sqrt{36^2+15^2}=39,\n\\]\nand its line has equation \\(5X-12Y=0\\).\n\nFor an integer point \\(C=(x,y)\\), the point-to-line distance formula gives the height\n\\[\nh=\\frac{|5x-12y|}{\\sqrt{5^2+12^2}}\n=\\frac{|5x-12y|}{13}.\n\\]\nThe numerator is an integer. It cannot be zero because the three vertices form a triangle, so \\(h\\ge\\frac1{13}\\). Consequently,\n\\[\nK=\\frac12(39)h\\ge\\frac{39}{26}=\\frac32.\n\\]\nFor \\(C=(5,2)\\), the numerator is \\(|25-24|=1\\), so this height and area are attained. The minimum area is \\(\\boxed{\\frac32}\\), choice C.",
