"label": "Work backward with equal groups",
"explanation": "Work backward from the \\(12\\) people who were not dancing. One third of those remaining danced, so the nondancers made up two of three equal groups.\n\nThose two groups contained \\(12\\) people, so each group contained \\(12\\div2=6\\) people. All three groups together therefore contained\n\\[\n3\\times6=18\\text{ people}.\n\\]\nThese \\(18\\) people were the half who stayed. Doubling gives the original number:\n\\[\n2\\times18=36.\n\\]\nThe room originally contained \\(36\\) people, choice C.",
