"solution": "Using the same number of disks for buying and selling makes the profit easy to compare. The smallest batch that contains whole groups of both \\(4\\) and \\(3\\) disks has \\(12\\) disks.\n\nBuying \\(12\\) disks costs \\(3\\cdot\\$5=\\$15\\), while selling them brings in \\(4\\cdot\\$5=\\$20\\). The profit is therefore \\(\\$20-\\$15=\\$5\\) per batch. Since both cost and revenue scale with the number of disks, earning \\(\\$100\\) requires \\(100\\div5=20\\) such batches. The number of disks is\n\\[\n20\\cdot12=\\boxed{240},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
