"label": "Find the profit per disk",
"explanation": "The buying and selling rates give the cost and revenue for one disk. Each disk costs \\(\\frac54\\) dollars and sells for \\(\\frac53\\) dollars, so the profit per disk is\n\\[\n\\frac53-\\frac54\n=\\frac{20-15}{12}\n=\\frac5{12}\\text{ dollars}.\n\\]\nTo earn \\(100\\) dollars, Maria must sell\n\\[\n100\\div\\frac5{12}\n=100\\cdot\\frac{12}{5}\n=\\boxed{240}\n\\]\ndisks. This quantity is divisible by both \\(4\\) and \\(3\\), so it can be bought and sold in complete stated groups. The answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
