"explanation": "The ratio gives \\(2\\) parts boys and \\(3\\) parts girls, so the whole class has \\(2+3=5\\) equal parts. Therefore the fraction of students who are boys is\n\\[\n\\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{40}{100}=40\\%.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(40\\%\\), choice C.",
