"label": "Compare the effects of the operations",
"explanation": "Since \\(0<\\frac1{2468}<1\\), subtracting this fraction from \\(13579\\) or multiplying \\(13579\\) by it gives a number below \\(13579\\). Adding it gives a number below \\(13580\\), and \\(13579.2468\\) is also below \\(13580\\).\n\nDividing by a nonzero fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal. Therefore choice D is\n\\[\n13579\\div\\frac1{2468}=13579\\times2468\n>13579\\times2=27158.\n\\]\nThis exceeds every other choice, so the largest number is \\(\\boxed{13579\\div\\frac1{2468}}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
