"explanation": "A complex number is real exactly when its imaginary part is zero. Write \\(z=x+iy\\), where \\(x,y\\) are real, so that \\(z\\) corresponds to the point \\((x,y)\\). Using \\(i^2=-1\\),\n\\[\n(3+4i)(x+iy)\n=(3x-4y)+i(4x+3y).\n\\]\nThus the product is real exactly when\n\\[\n4x+3y=0,\n\\qquad\\text{or}\\qquad\n y=-\\frac43x.\n\\]\nThis is the equation of a line through the origin. Every point on that line makes the imaginary part zero, and every admissible point satisfies this equation. The origin is included because a product equal to zero is real.\n\nTherefore \\(S\\) is a \\(\\boxed{\\text{line}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
