"label": "Choose a trigonometric input directly",
"explanation": "The identity \\(\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta=1\\) suggests an input whose subtraction by \\(1\\) produces a cosine term. Choose\n\\[\nx=\\csc^2\\theta=\\frac1{\\sin^2\\theta}.\n\\]\nSince \\(0<\\theta<\\pi/2\\), both \\(\\sin^2\\theta\\) and \\(\\cos^2\\theta\\) are positive, and \\(0<\\sin^2\\theta<1\\). Thus \\(x>1\\), so the chosen input is allowed and every denominator below is nonzero.\n\nNow\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x}{x-1}\n&=\\frac{1/\\sin^2\\theta}{(1-\\sin^2\\theta)/\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\\n&=\\frac1{\\cos^2\\theta}\\\\\n&=\\sec^2\\theta.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nApplying the given rule at this \\(x\\) immediately yields\n\\[\nf(\\sec^2\\theta)=\\frac1x\n=\\boxed{\\sin^2\\theta},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
