"explanation": "The sum contains three equal addends, so it is three times \\(3^3\\). Expanding the power shows how many factors of \\(3\\) this gives:\n\\[\\begin{aligned}3^3+3^3+3^3&=3\\cdot3^3\\\\&=3\\cdot(3\\cdot3\\cdot3)\\\\&=3^4=81.\\end{aligned}\\]\nThe answer is \\(3^4\\), choice \\(\\mathrm A\\).",
