"rejectedAnswers": [],
"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "A penny, nickel, dime, and quarter are worth \\(1\\), \\(5\\), \\(10\\), and \\(25\\) cents. Their total is\n\\[\n1+5+10+25=41\\text{ cents}.\n\\]\nOne dollar is \\(100\\) cents, so Walter has \\(41/100=\\boxed{41\\%}\\) of a dollar, choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
