"solution": "Let the positive side lengths be \\(a,b,c\\). Each dimension occurs on four edges, so\n\\[\n4(a+b+c)=140,\n\\qquad a+b+c=35.\n\\]\nThe farthest corner is the opposite corner. Applying the Pythagorean theorem first across a face and then through the box gives\n\\[\na^2+b^2+c^2=21^2=441.\n\\]\nThe surface area is \\(S=2ab+2ac+2bc\\), since each rectangular face has an equal opposite face. These products appear when we square the dimension sum:\n\\[\n(a+b+c)^2=a^2+b^2+c^2+S.\n\\]\nTherefore\n\\[\nS=35^2-441=1225-441=\\boxed{784}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
