"label": "Use the circle's width",
"explanation": "The circle is \\(2\\cdot4=8\\) units across in every direction. In particular, its width measured perpendicular to a side of a containing square is \\(8\\), so the square's side length must be at least \\(8\\).\n\nA square of side \\(8\\), centered at the circle's center, contains the circle exactly between its opposite sides. Thus the smallest possible area is\n\\[\n8\\cdot8=64.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(64\\), choice D.",
