"question": "In triangle \\(ABC,\\) angle \\(C\\) is a right angle and \\(CB\\gt CA.\\) Point \\(D\\) is located on \\(\\overline{BC}\\) so that angle \\(CAD\\) is twice angle \\(DAB.\\) If \\(\\frac{AC}{AD}=\\frac{2}{3},\\) then \\(\\frac{CD}{BD}=\\frac{m}{n},\\) where \\(m\\) and \\(n\\) are relatively prime positive integers. Find \\(m+n.\\)",
