"explanation": "Label the rhombus \\(ABCD\\) in order so that \\(AC=24\\) and \\(BD=10\\), and let the diagonals meet at \\(O\\). They bisect each other at right angles, so\n\\[\nOA=12,\\qquad OB=5,\\qquad AB=\\sqrt{12^2+5^2}=13.\n\\]\nThe circle's center is equidistant from the two sides meeting at each vertex, so it lies on each internal angle bisector. A rhombus's diagonals bisect its vertex angles; consequently the circle's center is \\(O\\).\n\nLet \\(T\\) be the point where the circle touches \\(AB\\), and let its radius be \\(r\\). Then \\(OT=r\\) and \\(OT\\perp AB\\). Triangles \\(AOT\\) and \\(ABO\\) are similar: they share the angle between \\(AO\\) and \\(AB\\), and their angles at \\(T\\) and \\(O\\), respectively, are right angles. Matching corresponding sides gives\n\\[\n\\frac{OT}{OB}=\\frac{AO}{AB},\n\\qquad\n\\frac{r}{5}=\\frac{12}{13}.\n\\]\nHence \\(r=\\dfrac{60}{13}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
