"label": "Compare the five sums",
"explanation": "Compute each sum, keeping the negative signs and using a common denominator where needed:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{A: }&\\frac12+\\frac13+\\frac16=\\frac{3+2+1}{6}=1,\\\\\n\\text{B: }&2+(-2)+1=0+1=1,\\\\\n\\text{C: }&0.1+0.3+0.6=0.4+0.6=1,\\\\\n\\text{D: }&1.1+(-2.1)+1.0=-1+1=0,\\\\\n\\text{E: }&-\\frac32-\\frac52+5=-4+5=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nOnly the triplet in \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\) has a sum different from \\(1\\).",
