"label": "Compare the distances at four hours",
"explanation": "We need to compare the bikers at the same time. Find \\(4\\) on the horizontal hours axis and read the height of each biker's line there. Alberto has traveled about \\(60\\) miles, and Bjorn has traveled about \\(45\\) miles.\n\nTo find how many more miles Alberto has biked, subtract Bjorn's distance from Alberto's:\n\\[\n60-45=60-40-5=20-5=15.\n\\]\nAlberto has biked about \\(15\\) more miles, so the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
