"solution": "The given equation contains the same variables as the two ratios. Since \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are nonzero, divide \\(ab=a-b\\) first by \\(b\\) and then by \\(a\\):\n\\[\na=\\frac{a}{b}-1,\n\\qquad\nb=1-\\frac{b}{a}.\n\\]\nRearranging gives\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{b}=a+1,\n\\qquad\n\\frac{b}{a}=1-b.\n\\]\nThese substitutions remove both fractions from the requested expression:\n\\[\n\\frac{a}{b}+\\frac{b}{a}-ab\n=2+a-b-ab=2,\n\\]\nbecause \\(a-b=ab\\). Thus the value is \\(\\boxed{2}\\), choice E.",
