"label": "Check the reciprocals",
"explanation": "The reciprocal of a nonzero number \\(n\\) is \\(1/n\\). For \\(-2\\), the reciprocal is \\(-1/2\\), and\n\\[\n-2<-\\frac12.\n\\]\nThis inequality holds because \\(-2\\) lies farther left on the number line. The numbers \\(-1\\) and \\(1\\) equal their reciprocals, while \\(2>1/2\\). Zero has no reciprocal because multiplying zero by any number gives zero, never one. Thus the only qualifying number is \\(-2\\), choice A.",
