"explanation": "Because \\(x\\) has a reciprocal, \\(x\\ne0\\). Its reciprocal is \\(1/x\\), and its additive inverse is \\(-x\\). Their product simplifies to\n\\[\n\\frac1x(-x)=-1.\n\\]\nThe number is two more than this product, so \\(x=-1+2=1\\). Since \\(0<1\\le2\\), the number lies in \\(\\boxed{0<x\\le2}\\), choice C.",
