"explanation": "An even number must end in an even digit, so the last digit must be \\(2\\) or \\(4\\). For each ending, arrange the remaining digits in increasing order to make the number as small as possible. This works because, at the first place where two numbers differ, the smaller digit makes the smaller number.\n\nIf the last digit is \\(2\\), the smallest number is \\(13492\\). If the last digit is \\(4\\), the smallest number is \\(12394\\).\n\nThese cases cover every possible even ending. Since \\(12394<13492\\), the smallest allowed number is \\(12394\\). Its tens digit is \\(9\\), choice E.",
