"explanation": "Points \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) both have horizontal coordinate \\(3\\), so \\(AB\\) is vertical and has length \\(2-(-2)=4\\). Points \\(C\\) and \\(D\\) both have horizontal coordinate \\(-3\\), so \\(CD\\) is vertical and has length \\(0-(-2)=2\\).\n\nThese opposite sides are parallel, making \\(ABCD\\) a trapezoid. Their perpendicular separation is the horizontal distance \\(3-(-3)=6\\). Using the parallel sides as the bases, its area is\n\\[\n\\frac{4+2}{2}\\times6=18.\n\\]\nThe area is \\(18\\) square units, choice C.",
