"solution": "First find how many students prefer cherry pie. Chocolate, apple, and blueberry account for \\(12+8+6=26\\) students, leaving \\(36-26=10\\). Half of these, or \\(5\\) students, prefer cherry.\n\nThe full pie graph has \\(360^\\circ\\) and represents \\(36\\) students, so each student accounts for \\(360^\\circ\\div36=10^\\circ\\). Cherry pie therefore needs\n\\[\n5\\times10^\\circ=50^\\circ.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{50^\\circ}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
