"label": "Choose a value that always works",
"explanation": "We need only one suitable positive integer \\(n\\) for each \\(m\\). Choose \\(n=1\\). Then, for every positive integer \\(m\\),\n\\[\nmn=m\\le m+1=m+n.\n\\]\nThus every positive integer \\(m\\) qualifies. Since there are infinitely many positive integers, the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{infinitely many}}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
