"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "Let the middle integer be \\(m\\), so the three integers are \\(m-1,m,m+1\\), with \\(m\\ge2\\). Their sum is \\(3m\\), which makes the given condition\n\\[\nm(m-1)(m+1)=8(3m)=24m.\n\\]\nBecause \\(m>0\\), division by \\(m\\) is valid and gives\n\\[\n(m-1)(m+1)=24.\n\\]\nThus the two outer integers are positive factors of \\(24\\) that differ by \\(2\\).\n\nThe smaller factor must be at most \\(4\\), since \\(5\\cdot5>24\\). Checking smaller factors \\(1,2,3,4\\) gives all positive factor pairs:\n\\[\n(1,24),\\ (2,12),\\ (3,8),\\ (4,6).\n\\]\nOnly \\((4,6)\\) has difference \\(2\\). Hence the three integers are \\(4,5,6\\). They satisfy the original condition because \\(4\\cdot5\\cdot6=120=8(4+5+6)\\). Their squares sum to\n\\[\n4^2+5^2+6^2=16+25+36=\\boxed{77},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
