"id": "reciprocal-am-gm",
"label": "Bound two positive reciprocal quantities",
"explanation": "Let \\(u=\\log_a b\\) and \\(v=\\log_b a\\). Both are positive because \\(a,b>1\\), and change of base shows\n\\[\nuv=\\frac{\\log b}{\\log a}\n\\frac{\\log a}{\\log b}=1.\n\\]\nThe quotient rule rewrites the requested expression as\n\\[\n\\log_a\\left(\\frac ab\\right)\n+\\log_b\\left(\\frac ba\\right)=2-u-v.\n\\]\nFor the positive numbers \\(u\\) and \\(v\\), AM-GM gives\n\\[\nu+v\\ge2\\sqrt{uv}=2.\n\\]\nThus the expression is at most zero. Equality requires \\(u=v\\); together with \\(uv=1\\) and positivity, this gives \\(u=v=1\\), or \\(a=b\\). Taking \\(a=b=2\\) attains equality, so the largest value is \\(\\boxed{0}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
