"explanation": "Equal amounts of dough at the same thickness give Art's and Roger's batches the same total cookie area. Their individual cookie areas, in square inches, are\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{Art: }&\\frac{(3+5)\\cdot3}{2}=12,\\\\\n\\text{Roger: }&4\\cdot2=8.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nArt makes \\(12\\) cookies, so each batch has total cookie area \\(12\\cdot12=144\\) square inches. Roger therefore makes \\(144\\div8=18\\) cookies.\n\nArt's batch earns \\(12\\cdot60=720\\) cents. To earn the same total from Roger's \\(18\\) cookies, the price of each must be\n\\[\n720\\div18=40\\text{ cents}.\n\\]\nRoger should charge \\(40\\)¢ per cookie, choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
