"explanation": "Convert the tax percentage to a decimal:\n\\[\n1.45\\%=\\frac{1.45}{100}=0.0145.\n\\]\nMultiplying the hourly wage by this fraction gives the tax in dollars per hour:\n\\[\n20\\cdot0.0145=0.29.\n\\]\nSince one dollar is \\(100\\) cents, \\(0.29\\) dollars is \\(\\boxed{29}\\) cents. The answer is choice \\(\\text{E}\\).",
