"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "The quantities \\(|x-1|\\) and \\(|x-2|\\) are the distances from \\(x\\) to \\(1\\) and \\(2\\) on the number line. We need these distances to be equal.\n\nIf \\(x\\leq1\\), then \\(2\\) is one unit farther away than \\(1\\). If \\(x\\geq2\\), then \\(1\\) is one unit farther away than \\(2\\). Between the two numbers, equal distances occur exactly halfway between them. Therefore\n\\[\nx=\\frac{1+2}{2}=\\frac32.\n\\]\nBoth distances are then \\(\\frac12\\). Thus \\(\\boxed{x=\\frac32}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
