"id": "equal-or-opposite",
"label": "Use equal or opposite expressions",
"explanation": "Two real numbers with equal absolute values must be equal or opposites, because absolute value records magnitude without the sign. Thus there are two possibilities:\n\\[\nx-1=x-2\n\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\nx-1=-(x-2).\n\\]\nThe first would give \\(-1=-2\\), which is impossible. The second gives\n\\[\nx-1=2-x,\n\\qquad 2x=3,\n\\qquad x=\\frac32.\n\\]\nSubstituting into the original equation gives \\(|\\frac12|=|-\\frac12|\\), so this value works. The two cases cover every possibility, hence the unique answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac32}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
