"explanation": "First find the maximum heart rate, because the target is a percentage of that number. For a \\(26\\)-year-old athlete, the maximum is\n\\[\n220-26=194\n\\]\nbeats per minute. Since \\(80\\%=0.8\\), the target is\n\\[\n0.8\\times194=155.2\n\\]\nbeats per minute. The tenths digit is \\(2\\), so rounding to the nearest whole number gives \\(155\\) beats per minute, choice B.",
