"id": "groups-of-rotations",
"label": "Average groups of five rotations",
"explanation": "Group a number with the four numbers obtained by repeatedly moving its first digit to the end. All five numbers remain valid five-digit numbers because none of the digits is zero. They are distinct because their first digits are distinct.\n\nThese groups partition all the numbers: every number belongs to a group, and rotating any member produces exactly the same five members, so two groups cannot partly overlap.\n\nWithin each group, every digit appears once in each position. The sum of the five numbers is therefore\n\\[\n(1+3+5+7+8)(10000+1000+100+10+1)\n=24\\cdot11111.\n\\]\nEvery group has mean\n\\[\n\\frac{24\\cdot11111}{5}=53332.8.\n\\]\nCombining groups with this same mean leaves the overall mean unchanged. The answer is \\(53332.8\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
