"label": "Find the side from the common perimeter",
"explanation": "The equal perimeters let us use the triangle's sides to find the square's perimeter:\n\\[\n6.1+8.2+9.7=24\\text{ cm}.\n\\]\nA square has four equal sides, so each side is \\(24\\div4=6\\) cm. Its area is therefore\n\\[\n6\\times6=\\boxed{36}\\text{ cm}^2,\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\text{C}\\).",
