"id": "remove-increases",
"label": "Remove the increases above the first day's amount",
"explanation": "Compared with May \\(1\\), the extra bananas eaten on the five days are \\(0,6,12,18,24\\). These extras total\n\\[\n0+6+12+18+24=60.\n\\]\nRemoving them from the \\(100\\) bananas leaves \\(100-60=40\\). This remainder consists of five copies of the May \\(1\\) amount, so Big Al ate \\(40\\div5=8\\) bananas on May \\(1\\).\n\nMay \\(5\\) comes after four increases of \\(6\\), so its count is\n\\[\n8+4\\times6=\\boxed{32}\n\\]\nbananas, choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
