"label": "Compare their clockwise progress",
"explanation": "Since only their stopping points matter, replace Bob's move of \\(9\\) points counterclockwise by the equivalent move of\n\\[\n12-9=3\n\\]\npoints clockwise. Both moves end at the same point on this twelve-point circle.\n\nViewed this way, Alice moves \\(5\\) points clockwise each turn while Bob moves \\(3\\), so Alice gains \\(2\\) points per turn. They start together and stop together again exactly when her accumulated gain is a whole number of twelve-point circuits.\n\nAfter the first six turns, her gains are\n\\[\n2,\\ 4,\\ 6,\\ 8,\\ 10,\\ 12.\n\\]\nThe first five gains are not complete circuits, while the sixth is exactly one circuit. Thus their first common stopping point after play begins occurs after \\(\\boxed{6}\\) turns, choice A.",
