"label": "Use the difference",
"explanation": "Consecutive odd integers differ by \\(2\\). Since the larger integer is three times the smaller, subtracting the smaller leaves twice the smaller. Thus twice the smaller integer is \\(2\\), so the smaller is \\(2\\div2=1\\). The larger is then \\(3\\cdot1=3\\).\n\nThese are consecutive odd integers satisfying the condition. Their sum is \\(1+3=\\boxed{4}\\), choice A.",
