"label": "Count ordered selections and remove repetition",
"explanation": "Temporarily select the three blocks in order. There are \\(25\\) choices for the first block. After its row and column are excluded, the second block has \\(4\\cdot4=16\\) possible positions. After two valid choices, three rows and three columns remain available, giving \\(3\\cdot3=9\\) choices for the third block.\n\nThis gives \\(25\\cdot16\\cdot9\\) ordered selections. Every valid group of three distinct blocks appears in exactly \\(3\\cdot2\\cdot1=6\\) orders. Conversely, each counted ordered selection produces a valid group. Therefore the required number is\n\\[\n\\frac{25\\cdot16\\cdot9}{6}=600,\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(C\\).",
