"label": "Compare the difference",
"explanation": "Consecutive odd integers differ by \\(2\\). Since the larger integer is three times the smaller, subtracting the smaller from the larger leaves twice the smaller. Therefore the smaller integer is\n\\[\n2\\div(3-1)=1.\n\\]\nThe larger is \\(3\\), and \\(1\\) and \\(3\\) are indeed consecutive odd integers. Their sum is \\(1+3=4\\), choice A.",
