"explanation": "On the unit circle, sine is the vertical coordinate. Points with the same vertical coordinate have angles \\(x\\) and \\(\\pi-x\\), allowing whole turns of \\(2\\pi\\). These account for every point with that height, so \\(\\sin x=\\sin nx\\) holds exactly when\n\\[\nnx=x+2k\\pi\n\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\nnx=\\pi-x+2j\\pi,\n\\]\nwhere \\(k,j\\) are integers. Since \\(n>1\\), solving these equations gives two families:\n\\[\nx=\\frac{2k\\pi}{n-1},\n\\qquad\nx=\\frac{(2j+1)\\pi}{n+1}.\n\\]\nThe closed interval \\([0,\\pi]\\) imposes\n\\[\n0\\le k\\le\\frac{n-1}{2},\n\\qquad\n0\\le j\\le\\frac n2.\n\\]\nThese non-strict bounds include all endpoint solutions.\n\nIf \\(n=2m\\), the families contain \\(m\\) and \\(m+1\\) entries. If \\(n=2m+1\\), they contain \\(m+1\\) entries each. Either way, their counts add to \\(n+1\\). Within each family, different indices give different values.\n\nWe must still remove any value appearing in both families. If both angle equations hold, subtracting them gives\n\\[\n2x=\\pi+2(j-k)\\pi.\n\\]\nThe only such value in \\([0,\\pi]\\) is \\(x=\\pi/2\\). It belongs to both families exactly when \\(k=j=(n-1)/4\\) is an integer, that is, when \\(n=4r+1\\) for an integer \\(r\\ge1\\). Thus \\(F(n)=n+1\\), with one subtraction for each such \\(n\\).\n\nSumming the initial counts gives\n\\[\n\\sum_{n=2}^{2007}(n+1)\n=\\frac{2006(3+2008)}2\n=2{,}017{,}033.\n\\]\nThe indices requiring a subtraction are \\(5,9,\\ldots,2005\\), of which there are\n\\[\n\\frac{2005-5}{4}+1=501.\n\\]\nTherefore the requested sum is\n\\[\n2{,}017{,}033-501=\\boxed{2{,}016{,}532},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
