"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "The \\(25\\%\\) comparison uses the blue count as its base. If \\(b\\) is the number of blue marbles, then the red count is \\(125\\%\\) of \\(b\\), so\n\\[\nr=1.25b,\n\\qquad\nb=\\frac{r}{1.25}=0.8r.\n\\]\nThe green count is \\(60\\%\\) more than the red count, so it is\n\\[\nr+0.60r=1.6r.\n\\]\nAdding the three colors gives\n\\[\nr+0.8r+1.6r=\\boxed{3.4r}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
