"label": "Start with five two-point baskets",
"explanation": "Five two-point baskets give \\(5\\cdot2=10\\) points. Replacing a two-point basket with a three-point basket increases the total by exactly \\(1\\).\n\nThe number of three-point baskets can be \\(0,1,2,3,4,\\) or \\(5\\), producing exactly the distinct totals\n\\[\n10,\\ 11,\\ 12,\\ 13,\\ 14,\\ 15.\n\\]\nEvery scoring pattern has one of these six numbers of three-point baskets, and each number is possible. Therefore, there are \\(\\boxed{6}\\) different totals, choice \\(\\text{E}\\).",
