"label": "Scale equivalent quantities",
"explanation": "Equivalent quantities of fruit scale by the same factor. The given quantity of bananas is \\(\\frac23\\cdot10=\\frac{20}{3}\\), and the requested quantity is \\(\\frac12\\cdot5=\\frac52\\).\n\nLet \\(o\\) be the number of oranges worth as much as the requested bananas. Comparing the banana quantities gives the proportion\n\\[\n\\frac{o}{8}=\\frac{5/2}{20/3}=\\frac52\\cdot\\frac3{20}=\\frac38.\n\\]\nThus \\(o=8\\cdot\\frac38=3\\). The answer is \\(3\\) oranges, choice C.",
