"solution": "Measuring both points from \\(D\\) lets us find \\(BC\\) by subtracting two lengths. Let \\(L=AD>0\\).\n\nBecause \\(AB=4BD\\), the whole segment \\(AD=AB+BD\\) consists of five equal parts of length \\(BD\\). Therefore \\(BD=L/5\\). Similarly, \\(AC=9CD\\) makes \\(AD=AC+CD\\) ten equal parts of length \\(CD\\), so \\(CD=L/10\\).\n\nSince \\(BD>CD\\), point \\(C\\) lies between \\(B\\) and \\(D\\). Hence\n\\[\nBC=BD-CD=\\frac{L}{5}-\\frac{L}{10}=\\frac{L}{10}.\n\\]\nDividing by \\(AD=L>0\\), the requested fraction is \\(\\boxed{\\tfrac{1}{10}}\\), choice C.",
