"label": "Split the closing speed",
"explanation": "Because Andrea and Lauren bike toward each other, their speeds add to the rate at which the distance between them decreases. Their speeds are in the ratio \\(3:1\\), so Lauren's speed is\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3+1}=\\frac14\n\\]\nkilometer per minute.\n\nDuring the first \\(5\\) minutes, their separation decreases by \\(5\\cdot1=5\\) kilometers. They are therefore still \\(20-5=15\\) kilometers apart when Andrea stops. Lauren must cover this remaining distance alone, taking\n\\[\n15\\div\\frac14=60\n\\]\nmore minutes. Including the first \\(5\\) minutes, the total time is \\(5+60=\\boxed{65}\\) minutes, choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
