"label": "Use equal areas to find parallel sides",
"explanation": "Adding the area of \\(\\triangle AEB\\) to each of the given equal areas shows that \\(\\triangle ABD\\) and \\(\\triangle ABC\\) have equal areas. They share the positive base \\(AB\\), so their perpendicular heights from \\(D\\) and \\(C\\) to \\(AB\\) are equal.\n\nBecause \\(ABCD\\) is convex, \\(C\\) and \\(D\\) lie on the same side of \\(AB\\). Points at the same positive perpendicular distance on one side of a line lie on a parallel line. Hence \\(CD\\parallel AB\\).\n\nNow \\(\\angle AEB=\\angle CED\\) are vertical angles, and \\(\\angle ABE=\\angle CDE\\) are alternate interior angles formed by the parallel lines. Therefore \\(\\triangle AEB\\) and \\(\\triangle CED\\) are similar by angle-angle similarity. It follows that\n\\[\n\\frac{AE}{EC}=\\frac{AB}{CD}=\\frac9{12}=\\frac34.\n\\]\nSince \\(E\\) lies between \\(A\\) and \\(C\\), the length \\(AC=14\\) consists of \\(3+4=7\\) proportional parts. Thus\n\\[\nAE=\\frac37\\cdot14=\\boxed6,\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\text{E}\\).",
