"label": "Find the total, then replace muffins",
"explanation": "Five muffins would cost \\(5\\cdot50=250\\) cents, while five bagels would cost \\(5\\cdot75=375\\) cents. Thus Jane's total lies between \\(250\\) and \\(375\\) cents. The only whole-dollar amount in this interval is \\(300\\) cents.\n\nStarting with five muffins, each replacement by a bagel adds \\(75-50=25\\) cents. To increase the total from \\(250\\) to \\(300\\) cents requires\n\\[\n\\frac{300-250}{25}=\\boxed2\n\\]\nreplacements. Jane bought \\(2\\) bagels and \\(3\\) muffins, choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
