"explanation": "The area formula needs the radius, so first recover it from the circumference. Let \\(r>0\\) be the circle's radius. Using circumference \\(2\\pi r\\),\n\\[\n2\\pi r=24\\pi,\n\\qquad r=12.\n\\]\nThe area is therefore \\(\\pi r^2=\\pi\\cdot12^2=144\\pi\\). Comparing this with \\(k\\pi\\) gives \\(k=\\boxed{144}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
