"explanation": "To stop on draw \\(n\\), Isabella must draw white from boxes \\(1\\) through \\(n-1\\), then red from box \\(n\\). Reaching a box does not change its contents, so the relevant probabilities at box \\(k\\) are \\(k/(k+1)\\) for white and \\(1/(k+1)\\) for red.\n\nFor \\(2\\le n\\le2010\\), multiplying these successive probabilities gives\n\\[\nP(n)=\\frac12\\cdot\\frac23\\cdots\n\\frac{n-1}{n}\\cdot\\frac1{n+1}\n=\\frac1{n(n+1)}.\n\\]\nThe consecutive factors cancel, leaving the first numerator and the final denominators. For \\(n=1\\), the probability is \\(1/2\\), which agrees with the same formula.\n\nAll denominators are positive, so\n\\[\nP(n)<\\frac1{2010}\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\nn(n+1)>2010.\n\\]\nThe product \\(n(n+1)\\) increases as the positive integer \\(n\\) increases. The decisive adjacent products are\n\\[\n44\\cdot45=1980<2010,\n\\qquad\n45\\cdot46=2070>2010.\n\\]\nThus every \\(n\\le44\\) fails, while \\(n=45\\) works and is within the available boxes. The smallest value is \\(\\boxed{45}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
