"explanation": "Divide the required amount by the amount in one small bottle:\n\\[\n500=14\\times35+10.\n\\]\nThus \\(14\\) full small bottles provide \\(490\\) milliliters, leaving \\(10\\) milliliters still needed. Any smaller number provides even less, so at least \\(15\\) bottles are necessary.\n\nA fifteenth bottle contains enough to supply those last \\(10\\) milliliters; Jasmine can leave the rest in that bottle. Therefore the minimum is \\(\\boxed{15}\\) bottles, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
