"explanation": "The requested percentage uses the birds that are not swans as its whole. These birds account for\n\\[\n100\\%-25\\%=75\\%\n\\]\nof all the birds. All the geese belong to this group.\n\nBecause the given percentages refer to the same original total, that total cancels when we divide. The percentage of non-swans that are geese is therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{30}{75}\\cdot100\\%=40\\%.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(40\\%\\), choice C.",
