"label": "Split the region along the coordinate axes",
"explanation": "Because all four parameters are positive, both coordinate axes pass through the rectangle. Cutting the region along these axes produces four smaller rectangles.\n\nAbove the \\(x\\)-axis, the height is \\(a\\); the widths to the left and right of the \\(y\\)-axis are \\(c\\) and \\(d\\). These two areas are \\(ac\\) and \\(ad\\). Below the \\(x\\)-axis, the height is \\(b\\), giving areas \\(bc\\) and \\(bd\\).\n\nThe four pieces cover the entire region and have no overlapping interiors, so their areas add:\n\\[\n\\text{area}=ac+ad+bc+bd.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice A.",
