"label": "Evaluate the sums and use a common denominator",
"explanation": "First evaluate the two sums: \\(2+4+6=12\\) and \\(1+3+5=9\\). Both denominators are nonzero. Reduce the fractions, then use the common denominator \\(12\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{9}-\\frac9{12}\n=\\frac43-\\frac34\n=\\frac{16}{12}-\\frac9{12}\n=\\boxed{\\frac7{12}}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice C.",
