"solution": "Use the standard interpretation that each draw is uniform on \\([-20,10]\\). A product is positive exactly when both numbers are negative or both are positive.\n\nThe whole interval has length \\(30\\). Its negative portion has length \\(20\\), and its positive portion has length \\(10\\), so a single draw is negative with probability \\(2/3\\) and positive with probability \\(1/3\\). Drawing exactly zero has probability zero because a single point has length zero.\n\nIndependence lets us multiply the probabilities for the two draws. The two favorable cases cannot occur together, so their probabilities add:\n\\[\nP(\\text{positive product})\n=\\left(\\frac23\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac13\\right)^2\n=\\frac49+\\frac19\n=\\boxed{\\frac59}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
