"explanation": "Interpret both selections as uniform on \\([-20,10]\\). Represent the selected numbers by an ordered pair \\((u,v)\\). Because the selections are independent, the pair is uniform in the square\n\\[\n[-20,10]\\times[-20,10],\n\\]\nwhose area is \\(30^2=900\\).\n\nThe condition \\(uv>0\\) describes two disjoint regions. Both coordinates can be negative, giving a square of side \\(20\\), or both can be positive, giving a square of side \\(10\\). These have total area\n\\[\n20^2+10^2=500.\n\\]\nThe coordinate axes are excluded because they give product zero; excluding these line segments does not change area. Thus\n\\[\nP(uv>0)=\\frac{500}{900}=\\boxed{\\frac59},\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
