"id": "calculate-equal-share",
"label": "Calculate each person's equal share",
"explanation": "The total trip cost was\n\\[\n105+125+175=405\n\\]\ndollars. Sharing this equally among three people gives \\(405\\div3=135\\) dollars per person.\n\nTom must pay \\(t=135-105=30\\) dollars, and Dorothy must pay \\(d=135-125=10\\) dollars. Sammy then has a net cost of \\(175-30-10=135\\) dollars as well, so these payments do make all three costs equal. Hence\n\\[\nt-d=30-10=\\boxed{20},\n\\]\nchoice B.",
