"label": "Similar triangles",
"explanation": "The parallel segment \\(DE\\) makes triangle \\(BDE\\) similar to triangle \\(BAC\\). Indeed, they have the same angle at \\(B\\), and \\(DE\\parallel AC\\) gives \\(\\angle BDE=\\angle BAC\\), establishing similarity by two equal angles.\n\nCorresponding sides therefore satisfy\n\\[\n\\frac{BD}{BA}=\\frac{DE}{AC}.\n\\]\nBecause \\(BA=AC=28\\), this gives \\(BD=DE\\). Adding \\(AD\\) yields\n\\[\nAD+DE=AD+DB=AB=28.\n\\]\nOpposite sides of parallelogram \\(ADEF\\) are equal, so its perimeter is\n\\[\n2(AD+DE)=2\\cdot28=\\boxed{56},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\text{C}\\).",
