"responseType": "choice",
"question": "In triangle \\(\\triangle ABC,\\) \\(AB=13,\\) \\(BC=14,\\) and \\(CA=15.\\) Distinct points \\(D,\\) \\(E,\\) and \\(F\\) lie on segments \\(\\overline{BC},\\) \\(\\overline{CA},\\) and \\(\\overline{DE},\\) respectively, such that \\(\\overline{AD}\\perp\\overline{BC},\\) \\(\\overline{DE}\\perp\\overline{AC},\\) and \\(\\overline{AF}\\perp\\overline{BF}.\\) The length of segment \\(\\overline{DF}\\) can be written as \\(\\frac{m}{n},\\) where \\(m\\) and \\(n\\) are relatively prime positive integers. What is \\(m+n?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\( 18 \\)",
"B": "\\( 21 \\)",
"C": "\\( 24 \\)",
"D": "\\( 27 \\)",
"E": "\\( 30\\)"
},
"choiceOrder": [
"A",
"B",
"C",
"D",
"E"
],
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"acceptedResponses": [
"B"
],
"rejectedAnswers": [],
"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "The right angles at \\(D\\) and \\(F\\) suggest the circle with diameter \\(AB\\). First find the lengths needed to use that circle.\n\nLet \\(BD=d\\) and \\(AD=h\\). Since \\(DC=14-d\\), the two right triangles give\n\\[\nd^2+h^2=13^2,\n\\qquad\n(14-d)^2+h^2=15^2.\n\\]\nSubtracting eliminates \\(h^2\\), giving \\(196-28d=56\\). Thus\n\\[\nBD=5,\\qquad DC=9,\\qquad AD=12.\n\\]\n\nTriangles \\(ADE\\) and \\(ACD\\) share their angle at \\(A\\) and have right angles at \\(E\\) and \\(D\\), respectively. They are similar, with\n\\[\n\\frac{AE}{AD}=\\frac{DE}{CD}=\\frac{AD}{AC}=\\frac{12}{15}.\n\\]\nConsequently,\n\\[\nAE=\\frac{48}{5},\n\\qquad\nDE=\\frac{36}{5}.\n\\]\n\nBecause \\(\\angle ADB=\\angle AFB=90^\\circ\\), the points \\(A,B,D,F\\) lie on the circle with diameter \\(AB\\). Also, \\(F\\) lies strictly between \\(D\\) and \\(E\\), so \\(FE\\) extends \\(FD\\). The opposite angles of cyclic quadrilateral \\(ABDF\\) are supplementary, giving\n\\[\n\\angle EFA\n=180^\\circ-\\angle DFA\n=\\angle ABD.\n\\]\nTogether with the right angles at \\(E\\) and \\(D\\), this proves \\(\\triangle AEF\\sim\\triangle ADB\\). Therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{EF}{BD}=\\frac{AE}{AD}=\\frac45,\n\\qquad EF=4.\n\\]\nIt follows that\n\\[\nDF=DE-EF=\\frac{36}{5}-4=\\frac{16}{5}.\n\\]\nThe integers \\(16\\) and \\(5\\) are relatively prime, so \\(m+n=\\boxed{21}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
