"label": "Make the counts equal",
"explanation": "With one additional nickel, Leah would have \\(14\\) coins, split equally between pennies and nickels. She would therefore have \\(14\\div2=7\\) of each.\n\nRemoving that hypothetical nickel leaves \\(7\\) pennies and \\(6\\) nickels. A penny is worth \\(1\\) cent and a nickel is worth \\(5\\) cents, so her original coins are worth\n\\[\n7\\cdot1+6\\cdot5=7+30=\\boxed{37}\\text{ cents},\n\\]\nchoice C.",
