"question": "The number \\(5^{867}\\) is between \\(2^{2013}\\) and \\(2^{2014}.\\) How many pairs of integers \\((m,n)\\) are there such that \\(1\\le m\\le2012\\) and \\[5^n\\lt2^m\\lt2^{m+2}\\lt5^{n+1}?\\]",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\(278\\)",
"B": "\\(279\\)",
"C": "\\(280\\)",
"D": "\\(281\\)",
"E": "\\(282\\)"
},
"choiceOrder": [
"A",
"B",
"C",
"D",
"E"
],
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "B",
"acceptedResponses": [
"B"
],
"rejectedAnswers": [],
"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "For each \\(m\\), the number \\(2^m\\) lies in exactly one gap between consecutive powers of \\(5\\). It gives a valid pair precisely when \\(2^{m+2}\\) remains in that same gap. Thus we can count the starting exponents \\(m\\) whose window crosses a power of \\(5\\).\n\nThere are \\(2012\\) possible values of \\(m\\). No endpoint \\(2^m\\) or \\(2^{m+2}\\) equals a positive power of \\(5\\), since the former is even and the latter is odd. Also, a window \\((2^m,2^{m+2})\\) cannot contain two powers of \\(5\\): its endpoints have ratio \\(4\\), whereas two distinct powers of \\(5\\) have ratio at least \\(5\\).\n\nSuppose\n\\[\n2^r<5^j<2^{r+1}.\n\\]\nExactly two unrestricted windows cross this power, those starting at \\(m=r-1\\) and \\(m=r\\).\n\nFor \\(1\\le j\\le866\\), we have \\(5^j\\ge5>2^2\\), and the given upper bound implies\n\\[\n5^{866}<\\frac{2^{2014}}5<2^{2012}.\n\\]\nHence \\(2\\le r\\le2011\\), so both excluded values \\(r-1,r\\) lie in the allowed range. These powers exclude \\(2\\cdot866\\) windows.\n\nThe given power \\(5^{867}\\) lies between \\(2^{2013}\\) and \\(2^{2014}\\), so it crosses the windows starting at \\(2012\\) and \\(2013\\); only \\(2012\\) is allowed. Higher powers exceed \\(2^{2014}\\), and powers with nonpositive exponent are below every window.\n\nAll forbidden windows have therefore been counted, and none was counted twice. Each remaining \\(m\\) determines one \\(n\\), so the number of pairs is\n\\[\n2012-2\\cdot866-1=\\boxed{279},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
