"label": "Find the time for one task",
"explanation": "The interval from \\(1{:}00\\) PM to \\(2{:}40\\) PM covers exactly two tasks. It lasts \\(60+40=100\\) minutes. Since the tasks take equal amounts of time, each takes\n\\[\n100\\div2=50\\text{ minutes}.\n\\]\nThe third task ends \\(50\\) minutes after \\(2{:}40\\) PM, which is \\(\\boxed{3{:}30\\text{ PM}}\\), choice B.",
