"label": "Bound the smaller integer",
"explanation": "The ordering gives a short list of possible values for \\(y\\). If \\(y\\geq8\\), then the integer \\(x>y\\) must satisfy \\(x\\geq9\\), giving\n\\[\nx+y+xy\\geq9+8+9\\cdot8=89,\n\\]\nwhich contradicts the required total of \\(80\\). Hence \\(y\\) must be one of \\(1,2,3,4,5,6,7\\).\n\nFor each of these values, substitution into the original equation gives a simple equation for \\(x\\):\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x&=79 &&(y=1),\\\\\n3x&=78 &&(y=2),\\\\\n4x&=77 &&(y=3),\\\\\n5x&=76 &&(y=4),\\\\\n6x&=75 &&(y=5),\\\\\n7x&=74 &&(y=6),\\\\\n8x&=73 &&(y=7).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nOnly \\(3x=78\\) has an integer solution, because in every other equation the coefficient of \\(x\\) does not divide the right side. Thus \\(y=2\\) and \\(x=26\\). Each possible \\(y\\) was checked, and each determines at most one \\(x\\), so the search is complete. Since \\(26>2>0\\) and \\(26+2+52=80\\), the answer is \\(\\boxed{26}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
