"explanation": "Convert both dimensions to yards so their product will be in square yards. Since \\(3\\) feet make \\(1\\) yard, the floor is \\(12\\div3=4\\) yards long and \\(9\\div3=3\\) yards wide. A rectangle's area is length times width, so the carpet required is\n\\[\n4\\cdot3=\\boxed{12}\\text{ square yards},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
