"label": "Count the odd products",
"explanation": "It is convenient to count the products that are odd and subtract them from all possible outcomes. A product is odd exactly when both factors are odd.\n\nThere are \\(3\\times3=9\\) equally likely ordered pairs, recording the number from each separate box. Each box has two odd chips, numbered \\(1\\) and \\(3\\), so there are \\(2\\times2=4\\) odd-product pairs. Pairing each first-box choice with each second-box choice includes every such outcome exactly once.\n\nEvery product is either odd or even, so the remaining \\(9-4=5\\) outcomes have even products. The required probability is\n\\[\n\\frac{9-4}{9}=\\boxed{\\frac59},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\text{E}\\).",
