"skill": [],
"responseType": "choice",
"question": "In regular hexagon \\(ABCDEF,\\) points \\(W,\\) \\(X,\\) \\(Y,\\) and \\(Z\\) are chosen on sides \\(\\overline{BC},\\) \\(\\overline{CD},\\) \\(\\overline{EF},\\) and \\(\\overline{FA}\\) respectively, so lines \\(AB,\\) \\(ZW,\\) \\(YX,\\) and \\(ED\\) are parallel and equally spaced. What is the ratio of the area of hexagon \\(WCXYFZ\\) to the area of hexagon \\(ABCDEF?\\)",
"questionType": "text",
"choices": {
"A": "\\( \\ \\dfrac{1}{3} \\)",
"B": "\\( \\ \\dfrac{10}{27} \\)",
"C": "\\( \\ \\dfrac{11}{27} \\)",
"D": "\\( \\ \\dfrac{4}{9} \\)",
"E": "\\( \\ \\dfrac{13}{27} \\)"
},
"choiceOrder": [
"A",
"B",
"C",
"D",
"E"
],
"choicesType": "text",
"answer": "C",
"acceptedResponses": [
"C"
],
"rejectedAnswers": [],
"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "The desired hexagon is what remains after removing the trapezoids next to \\(AB\\) and \\(ED\\). Equal spacing gives their heights, so we only need their parallel side lengths.\n\nLet the regular hexagon's side length be \\(s>0\\), and let the perpendicular distance between \\(AB\\) and \\(ED\\) be \\(H>0\\). Joining the center to the six vertices gives six equilateral triangles. Consequently, the opposite-vertex diagonal \\(CF\\) has length \\(2s\\), and it is parallel to and halfway between \\(AB\\) and \\(ED\\).\n\nThe diagonal \\(CF\\) divides the original hexagon into two trapezoids, each with bases \\(s,2s\\) and height \\(H/2\\). Therefore its total area is\n\\[\n2\\cdot\\frac{s+2s}{2}\\cdot\\frac H2\n=\\frac{3sH}{2}.\n\\]\nThe side locations place \\(ZW\\) above \\(CF\\) and \\(YX\\) below it. Since the four given lines are equally spaced, \\(ZW\\) is \\(H/3\\) from \\(AB\\). This is a fraction\n\\[\n\\frac{H/3}{H/2}=\\frac23\n\\]\nof the distance from \\(AB\\) to \\(CF\\). By proportional segments cut by parallel lines, the two straight sides produce the same fraction of the width increase from \\(s\\) to \\(2s\\). Hence\n\\[\nZW=s+\\frac23(2s-s)=\\frac{5s}{3}.\n\\]\nBy the symmetry of the regular hexagon, \\(YX=5s/3\\) as well.\n\nEach removed trapezoid has bases \\(s,5s/3\\) and height \\(H/3\\), so its area is\n\\[\n\\frac{s+5s/3}{2}\\cdot\\frac H3=\\frac{4sH}{9}.\n\\]\nThe two removed pieces have disjoint interiors, leaving exactly \\(WCXYFZ\\). Thus the requested ratio is\n\\[\n\\frac{\\frac{3sH}{2}-2\\cdot\\frac{4sH}{9}}\n{\\frac{3sH}{2}}\n=\\boxed{\\frac{11}{27}},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{C}\\).",
