"explanation": "Because the two-digit numbers overlap, it helps to track the changes between neighboring digits. Comparing tens digits in \\(ab<bc<cd\\) shows that\n\\[\na\\le b\\le c.\n\\]\nIn particular, \\(b\\) and \\(c\\) are nonzero, as required for \\(bc\\) and \\(cd\\) to be two-digit integers.\n\nDefine\n\\[\nu=b-a,\\qquad v=c-b,\\qquad w=d-c.\n\\]\nThen \\(u,v\\ge0\\). Using place value, the two successive gaps are\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n(10b+c)-(10a+b)&=10u+v,\\\\\n(10c+d)-(10b+c)&=10v+w.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe arithmetic-sequence condition says these gaps are equal, so\n\\[\n10(u-v)=w-v.\n\\]\nSince all digits lie between 0 and 9, we have \\(-9\\le w\\le9\\) and \\(0\\le v\\le9\\). Therefore\n\\[\n-18\\le w-v\\le9.\n\\]\nThe only multiples of 10 in this interval are \\(-10\\) and 0. Thus either \\(v=u\\) or \\(v=u+1\\), which gives two exhaustive, disjoint cases.\n\nIf \\(v=u\\), the gap equation gives \\(w=u\\), so the digits are\n\\[\na,\\ a+u,\\ a+2u,\\ a+3u.\n\\]\nStrict increase of the two-digit numbers requires \\(u\\ge1\\). The last digit must be at most 9, giving \\(1\\le a\\le9-3u\\). For \\(u=1\\), there are 6 choices of \\(a\\); for \\(u=2\\), there are 3; larger \\(u\\) give none. This case contributes \\(6+3=9\\).\n\nIf \\(v=u+1\\), then \\(w=u-9\\), and the digits are\n\\[\na,\\ a+u,\\ a+2u+1,\\ a+3u-8.\n\\]\nThe bounds \\(c\\le9\\), \\(d\\ge0\\), and \\(a\\ge1\\) become\n\\[\n\\max(1,8-3u)\\le a\\le8-2u.\n\\]\nThese bounds require \\(u=0,1,2,3\\). Their possibilities are:\n\nFor \\(u=0\\), only \\(a=8\\) works, giving 1 number.\n\nFor \\(u=1\\), \\(a=5,6\\), giving 2 numbers.\n\nFor \\(u=2\\), \\(a=2,3,4\\), giving 3 numbers.\n\nFor \\(u=3\\), \\(a=1,2\\), giving 2 numbers.\n\nHere \\(d-c=u-9<0\\), so \\(d\\le9\\) follows from \\(c\\le9\\). The common two-digit gap is \\(10u+v=11u+1>0\\), so every listed choice satisfies strict increase. This case contributes \\(1+2+3+2=8\\).\n\nEach choice of \\(a,u,v\\) determines exactly one four-digit number. The two cases do not overlap, so the total is \\(9+8=\\boxed{17}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{D}\\).",
