"rejectedAnswers": [],
"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "Keep \\(9!\\) as a block and simplify the other factor first. Since \\(5!=120\\), the equation gives\n\n\\[\nN!=\\frac{5!\\cdot9!}{12}\n=\\frac{120}{12}\\cdot9!\n=10\\cdot9!\n=10!.\n\\]\n\nThus \\(N=\\boxed{10}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\). For these positive integers, multiplying by each next integer strictly increases the factorial, so no other offered value of \\(N\\) gives \\(10!\\). Recognizing the next factorial saves expanding the large product.",
