"label": "Count how many line sums contain each point",
"explanation": "Instead of finding all six digits, count how often each digit appears when the five line sums are added.\n\nThe figure shows these five sums:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&A+B+C,\\quad A+F+E,\\\\\n&B+D,\\quad B+F,\\quad C+D+E.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nEvery point appears twice except \\(B\\), which appears three times. The total is therefore\n\n\\[\n2(A+B+C+D+E+F)+B=47.\n\\]\n\nThe six digits are \\(1\\) through \\(6\\), so their sum is \\(21\\). Thus \\(42+B=47\\), giving \\(\\boxed{B=5}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\). Counting appearances reveals the extra copy of \\(B\\) without assigning the other digits.",
