"question": "Let \\(d(n)\\) denote the number of positive integers that divide \\(n,\\) including \\(1\\) and \\(n.\\) For example, \\(d(1) = 1,\\) \\(d(2) = 2,\\) and \\(d(12) = 6.\\) (This function is known as the divisor function.) Let \\[ f(n) = \\frac{d(n)}{\\sqrt[3]{n}}. \\]\n\nThere is a unique positive integer \\(N\\) such that \\(f(N) \\gt f(n)\\) for all positive integers \\(n \\ne N.\\) What is the sum of the digits of \\(N?\\)",
