"unorderedAnswers": false,
"solution": "Points \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) both have vertical coordinate \\(7\\), so \\(AB\\) is horizontal and has length \\(11-5=6\\). The corresponding height is the vertical distance from \\(C(3,y)\\) to \\((3,7)\\) on the line containing \\(AB\\). This is a valid height even though its foot lies to the left of \\(A\\).\n\nUsing triangle area equal to half the base times the height, the height \\(h\\) satisfies\n\\[\nh=\\frac{2\\cdot12}{6}=4.\n\\]\nSince \\(y>7\\), point \\(C\\) is four units above the horizontal line at height \\(7\\). Therefore \\(y=7+4=\\boxed{11}\\), choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
